I would like to know how to extract the nearest powers of ten concisely from this number. I have tried to use the floor function, but I am not sure if I am doing it correctly. Any help would be appreciated.

-
The floor function is the wrong tool to use here. You need to find the nearest power of ten. –  Brian M. Scott Feb 28 '12 at 19:32
@BrianM.Scott: I think he wants to extract the integer exponent k (e.g., -3 for 10^-3, 6 for 10^6) from the number. –  Aryabhata Feb 28 '12 at 19:35
@Aryabhata: Yes, I know that. I was just pointing out that the floor function is the wrong tool to use here. –  Brian M. Scott Feb 28 '12 at 19:36
@BrianM.Scott: I see. Thanks. –  Aryabhata Feb 28 '12 at 19:38

The nearest power of ten is $10^{\lfloor \log_{10} 13635428694 \rfloor}$.

